<title>LATVIA: INSURANCE PREMIUMS RISE IN FIRST HALF.</title>
<headline>INSURANCE PREMIUMS RISE IN FIRST HALF.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's insurance companies collected premiums worth 24.30 million lats in the first half of 1997, a rise of 12.4 percent or 8.2 million lats on the first half of 1996, the insurance inspectorate said on Monday.</p>
<p>The inspectorate said in a statement the largest life insurance company in terms of premiums was Salamandra Baltik. The second-placed life insurer was Ezerzeme and the third was was Latva.</p>
<p>The largest non-life company was Balta while second place was taken by Austrumu Alianse.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Lannin, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
